{{define "title"}}Someone asked to change your email address{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
{{/*
  NO LINK AND NO TOKEN. This message goes to the address a change is moving
  AWAY from, which is exactly the mailbox an attacker may already be reading; a
  credential in it would make the warning itself the attack. It also omits the
  new address, which would tell that attacker nothing they do not know and would
  tell everyone else where a stranger tried to send an account.
*/}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hello{{if .Name}} {{.Name}}{{end}},</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">Someone asked to move your Chronos account to a different email address. We are telling you here, at the address the account uses today, so that you hear about it even if the request was not yours.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">Nothing has changed. The move only happens if someone confirms a link we sent to the new address, and that link expires in {{.ExpiresIn}}.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;"><strong>If this was not you</strong>, sign in and cancel the request, then change your password. Someone with access to your account may have started this.</p>
<p style="margin:0;color:#6b7280;font-size:13px;">We have not included the new address or a link in this message. If your account has been reached by someone else, this message must not help them.</p>
{{end}}
